/-!
# Part II development entry point

Theorem A constructs the left proper combinatorial localization of the Reedy
model at the specified collapse family. Its fibrant objects are exactly the
homotopically constant Reedy fibrant diagrams, and constant diagrams and
evaluation at zero form a Quillen equivalence with the dagger Joyal model.

For Theorem B this target includes the change-of-index adjunctions, the
reversal Segal localizers, left proper combinatorial projective and injective
Kan diagram models, and the derived locality comparison for the left Kan
images of the resolved localizers. Standard frames identify strict and derived
mapping tests, yielding the strict and derived Segal-local object descriptions.
The localized model constructions and their Quillen equivalence remain in progress.
-/
